// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27os/update_probe.t27 -- a program that shows update_core.t27 + update_host.t27 working (Refs gHashTag/t27#11560).
// Headless, NOT the app: T27OS.app is never started. Prints one line per fact; the lines say what was OBSERVED.
// UP_ROLE (default table):
//   table     in memory (no ~/.t27os is read or written): two throw-away identities, a 2 MiB test file in $UP_DIR (default
//             /tmp): make a manifest, sign it, check it; flip one byte of every region; a stranger; a forged signature
//             under a friend's key; a rollback (build-1 and the same build); a size out of range; a truncated manifest; the
//             file hash and size; a second start while an update runs. Prints the table CASE | EXPECT | GOT.
//   announce  open (or make) the identity under $HOME/.t27os, register _t27call._udp with TXT fp/port/nick + ver/build, keep
//             it for UP_SECONDS. Run it with HOME=<an empty temp directory>.
//   browse    browse _t27call._udp for UP_SECONDS, resolve what is found and print each service with ver= and build= read
//             from its TXT record, and whether it runs a newer build than UP_BUILD.
//   both      announce and browse in one process.
// UP_SECONDS (default 8), UP_PORT (default 47741), UP_NICK (default t27os), UP_NAME (instance name, default the nick),
// UP_VERSION as a.b.c (default 0.1.3), UP_BUILD (default 4321), UP_DIR (default /tmp).
// Exit 0 only when every check this role makes passed.
// Build (Apple silicon):
//   t27b build specs/t27os/update_probe.t27 -o up.o --macho
//   ld -arch arm64 -platform_version macos 11.0 $(xcrun --show-sdk-version) -syslibroot $(xcrun --show-sdk-path) \
//      -e _main -lSystem -lffi -framework CoreFoundation -framework Security -o update_probe up.o
module T27osUpdateProbe;

